Yes, that too.

Hmm, all that needs some game balance, as "#curse
profusely" was originally intended (by me) merely to
be a tension reliever for the player, not for the
player character (PC).

Perhaps "cursing a blue streak" should, in exchange
for its alignment hit and monster awakening and/or
aggravation effects, give a Cherenkov radiation
"blue streak", a turn or two of temporary ESP _and_
magic mapping to the edge of the known game
universe, in a random octant or even quadrant in one
of the eight game directions?

With a timeout like a prayer timeout, this effect
could produce _misleading_ mapping/ESPing/both if
overused, or the blue streak could rebound and cause
damage to the PC.

Obviously, there would need to be a database of faux
curses produced in response to a "#curse profusely";
my particular favorite is "feldercarb", which IIRC
is from the "Battlestar Galactica" TV series.

